msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/standards.md
msgid "**adopt:** named in a contract clause;"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/standards.md
msgid "**reference:** a recommended method or background;"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/standards.md
msgid "**track:** watched, not yet relied on."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/standards.md
msgid "The register is [`blueprint/standards.yaml`]{1}; this page and the \"Standards\" section of each capability page are generated from it. Every entry was last checked on the date in the register. Entries checked as `catalogue` were confirmed from the publisher's catalogue listing because the publisher's page blocks automated reading; confirm them on the page before relying on the exact edition."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/standards.md
msgid "How standards are cited"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/standards.md
msgid "**Cite a dated edition with an \"or later\" rule** where newer editions stay compatible (for example \"OpenAPI 3.1 or later\"), so a patch release does not invalidate a clause."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/standards.md
msgid "**Separate the standard from its code list.** Country, currency and language codes change between editions through their maintenance agencies; each code list is loaded on a schedule, versioned, and recorded with its source and retrieval date ([CAP-REFERENCE]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/standards.md
msgid "**Prefer free, testable profiles in clauses** (RFC 3339 rather than the whole of ISO 8601), and cite the broader standard as background."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/standards.md
msgid "**Re-check the register at least once a year.** A new edition is a reviewed change to the register and, where it changes a clause, an ADR."
msgstr ""

